s8-p2 : Block
s8-p2 = prose (cons "The universal host does not erase the specificity of existing languages. A lifted C++ program must retain the distinctions made by its own standard—among permitted results, unspecified choices, undefined behavior, object lifetimes, and concurrent events—while becoming available to the host's operations on syntax, meaning, and evidence. The C++ language is specified by ISO/IEC 14882:2020 ([19](#ref-19)). Formal accounts of its concurrency and executable semantics, including the work of Batty and colleagues, provide relevant prior definitions ([20](#ref-20)). " nil)
